  "claims": [
    "Actual native conditional dead-store elimination, preserving four dependent oracle calls for every typed stateful probabilistic oracle.",
    "A complete final-frame refinement changes only final native program counter by +1, retaining all tapes, oracle state and bit transcript.",
    "Uniform stopping bound 343 to 286 transitions; checked constant-response witnesses refute old bound 342 and new bound 285.",
    "Two schematic local observation/compilation squares generate comparison for every plan of the existing serial MAC presentation.",
    "Generated diagram support is exactly original plan support; constructor bound is 12 times plan constructors, with one root generator per atom.",
    "Both proof-order routes emit identical optimized code and resource packet; hence their continuing timed executions agree at every horizon.",
    "The same ordinary rule library gives the identical complete ordinary tree and identical Option result of shared compilation. A concrete typed-claim check accepts both certificates, each with 56 nodes."
  ],
  "concrete_contract": {
    "old_instructions": 251,
    "new_instructions": 252,
    "old_uniform_bound_transitions": 343,
    "new_uniform_bound_transitions": 286,
    "oracle_calls": 4,
    "constant_zero_reply_branch_times": {
      "old": [
        285,
        343
      ],
      "new": [
        286,
        286
      ]
    },
    "serial_stage_3_example": {
      "root_generators": 4,
      "cell_constructors": 56,
      "guard_count": 1,
      "fresh_guards_for_change_1": 0,
      "geometric_certificate_accepted": true,
      "ordinary_certificate_accepted": true,
      "geometric_nodes": 56,
      "ordinary_nodes": 56
    }
  },
  "limits": [
    "Time includes caller and packet transfer, excludes oracle internals and initial key generation.",
    "The false branch increases from 285 to 286: no pointwise speed dominance or global optimality theorem.",
    "Code grows by one instruction; no code-size saving.",
    "Native implementation is certified for the existing fixed attack/source code, not a general optimizing compiler.",
    "The original and optimized clock processes differ; same-process theorem compares two routes producing the same optimized code.",
    "Quantitative error epsilon + 1/256 remains finite and fixed; no unconditional asymptotic-security promotion.",
    "The current transport concerns serial plans, not a full tensor/copy/discard mixed critical basis.",
    "Constructor counts exclude boundary payload, code, libraries, dependency search and model checking.",
    "Option compilation equality alone is not completeness; successful checked certificates are established for the concrete diagnostic.",
    "No intrinsic higher-dimensional compression is demonstrated: ordinary export is exactly equal under the common encoding.",
    "Compact native backend/internal oracle timing, scalable attacks and total-cost comparison remain open."
  ],
